C:\DocumentNoSnc\CC\GXEMUL\_scratchpad\ppc_pem_32and64_2005.txt:29992:Note: rlwimi can be used to insert a bit field into the contents of rA using the methods shown below:
C:\DocumentNoSnc\CC\GXEMUL\_scratchpad\ppc_pem_32and64_2005.txt:29993:� To insert an n-bit field, that is left-justified in the low-order 32 bits of rS, into the high-order 32 bits of rA starting at bit position b, set SH = 32 � b, MB = b, and ME = (b + n) � 1.
C:\DocumentNoSnc\CC\GXEMUL\_scratchpad\ppc_pem_32and64_2005.txt:29994:� To insert an n-bit field, that is right-justified in the low-order 32 bits of rS, into the high-order 32 bits of rA starting at bit position b, set SH = 32 � (b + n), MB = b, and ME = (b + n) � 1.
C:\DocumentNoSnc\CC\GXEMUL\_scratchpad\ppc_pem_32and64_2005.txt:30005:equivalent to rlwimi rA,rS,32 � b,b,b + n � 1
C:\DocumentNoSnc\CC\GXEMUL\_scratchpad\ppc_pem_32and64_2005.txt:30007:insrwi rA,rS,n,b (n > 0) equivalent to rlwimi rA,rS,32 � (b + n),b,(b + n) � 1
C:\DocumentNoSnc\CC\GXEMUL\_scratchpad\ppc_pem_32and64_2005.txt:30025:rlwinmx
