C:\DocumentNoSnc\CC\GXEMUL\_scratchpad\ppc_pem_32and64_2005.txt:30028:rlwinm rlwinm.
C:\DocumentNoSnc\CC\GXEMUL\_scratchpad\ppc_pem_32and64_2005.txt:30034:rlwinmx
C:\DocumentNoSnc\CC\GXEMUL\_scratchpad\ppc_pem_32and64_2005.txt:30065:The contents of rS[32-63] are rotated left the number of bits specified by operand SH. A mask is generated having 1 bits from bit MB + 32 through bit ME + 32 and 0 bits elsewhere. The rotated data is ANDed with the generated mask and the result is placed into rA. The upper 32 bits of rA are cleared.
C:\DocumentNoSnc\CC\GXEMUL\_scratchpad\ppc_pem_32and64_2005.txt:30067:Note: rlwinm can be used to extract, rotate, shift, and clear bit fields using the methods shown below:
C:\DocumentNoSnc\CC\GXEMUL\_scratchpad\ppc_pem_32and64_2005.txt:30068:� To extract an n-bit field, that starts at bit position b in the high-order 32 bits of rS, right-justified into rA (clearing the remaining 32 � n bits of rA), set SH = b + n, MB = 32 � n, and ME = 31.
C:\DocumentNoSnc\CC\GXEMUL\_scratchpad\ppc_pem_32and64_2005.txt:30069:� To extract an n-bit field, that starts at bit position b in the high-order 32 bits of rS, left-justified into rA (clearing the remaining 32 � n bits of rA), set SH = b, MB = 0, and ME = n � 1.
C:\DocumentNoSnc\CC\GXEMUL\_scratchpad\ppc_pem_32and64_2005.txt:30074:For all uses mentioned, the high-order 32 bits of rA are cleared.
C:\DocumentNoSnc\CC\GXEMUL\_scratchpad\ppc_pem_32and64_2005.txt:30087:rlwinm rA,rS,b,0,n � 1 rlwinm rA,rS,b + n,32 � n,31 rlwinm rA,rS,n,0,31 rlwinm rA,rS,32 � n,0,31 rlwinm rA,rS,n,0,31�n rlwinm rA,rS,32 � n,n,31 rlwinm rA,rS,0,n,31 rlwinm rA,rS,0,0,31 � n rlwinm rA,rS,n,b � n,31 � n
